From 4289d2e53d625d1784ec6373ae87e2d94c454ffa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 05:48:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(2d): air entry on the avoid route; pin 5 points at
 #3825

The avoid route (fixtures and clamps) now gives each level the start
side's air room, less that level's keep-outs over the whole descent, so
the Arc entry plunges in air and leads in clear of a clamp, or stands
down by name (#3810, folded in).

After the merge of #3818, four fig8 Outside pass links still lift across
the part to a start inside ring 0; the re-entries plunge, named. The
cause is the link code: the known-fail pin now names #3825. The
decision file records why Inside takes a named helix or ramp.

Refs #3746
Fixes #3810

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
